{
  "number": 681,
  "state": "closed",
  "title": "L3AF Delete API clears out all contents in l3af-config.json",
  "labels": [],
  "created_at": "2026-01-27T22:15:18Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-02-04T16:08:51Z",
  "closed_at": "2026-02-04T16:08:51Z",
  "body": "While using the delete API, the persistent /var/l3afd/l3af-config.json file clears out all the config even when deleting only one eBPF program out of many loaded on the host.

For example:
if 4 eBPF program loaded across two interfaces on Host A:

[
  {
    "host_name": "HOSTA",
    "iface": "tapX",
    "ipv4_address": "10.10.10.151",
    "bpf_programs": {
      "tc_ingress": [
        "program-a"
      ],
      "tc_egress": [
        "program-b"
      ]
    }
  },
  {
    "host_name": "ndc-appblx075-21-01",
    "iface": "tapY",
    "ipv4_address": "10.10.10.152",
    "bpf_programs": {
      "tc_ingress": [
        "program-a"
      ],
      "tc_egress": [
        "program-b"
      ]
    }
  }
]

When we call the deleted API to deleted the program only on tapX

curl -X POST http://localhost:7080/l3af/configs/v1/delete -d "@deletetapX.json"

[
    {
        "host_name": "HOSTA",
        "iface": "tapX",
        "ipv4_address": "10.10.10.151",
        "bpf_programs": {
            "tc_ingress": [
                "app-elb-agent"
            ],
            "tc_egress": [
                "app-elb-agent"
            ]
        }
    }
]

Although it appropriately deletes the programs, the l3af-config.json clears out all the programs in the file.

Rather it should delete the config for tapX and keep the configs for tapY as it is."
}

